{"id": "EUVD-2026-96562", "enisaUuid": "f905f849-5076-35b8-b2b2-ff57ed3c86e5", "description": "JeecgBoot through 3.9.5 contains a missing authorization vulnerability in the SysLogController deleteBatch handler that allows any authenticated user to delete system audit log entries. Low-privileged attackers can send a DELETE request with ids set to allclear to wipe the entire sys_log table, erasing all users' audit trails.", "datePublished": "2026-10-10T21:49:20", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T02:31:39", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:H/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/AnkesKasty/cve-request-poc/blob/a7b6d1423555812d8efa26c91c5d0683164b31e5/JeecgBoot/poc_log_delete_batch.py", "https://github.com/jeecgboot/JeecgBoot/blob/e3b9dc0aefe1943d9772b026f64ed671a7c82802/jeecg-boot/jeecg-module-system/jeecg-system-biz/src/main/java/org/jeecg/modules/system/controller/SysLogController.java#L125-L140", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/jeecgboot-through-3.9.5-missing-authorization-via-sys-log-deletebatch"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-108623", "GHSA-6vff-68pc-g8vm"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.3, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2d247d37-d4ca-3f7b-9360-5c49d530a69a", "product": {"name": "JeecgBoot", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22643.9.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "80e3b9db-5c77-3246-b8ed-eab00c3146a4", "vendor": {"name": "jeecgboot"}}], "isExploited": false}